# Service layers

## Contracted (`app/` + `app/impl/`)

The interface is the contract. Controllers inject that interface or a port — never
`@InternalService`. Name after the use case (`ProfileImageService` /
`ProfileImageServiceImpl`).

**JDBC-only:** put `@Transactional` (or `readOnly`) on the contracted impl and call
repositories there. Multiple repository calls in one method are one transaction.
Do not add an internal class.

## Internal (`app/internal/`, `@InternalService`)

Use **only** when the use case mixes outbound I/O (S3, HTTP, queues) with JDBC.
I/O stays on the contracted impl; JDBC stays on this bean so the transaction does
not wrap the I/O. Name after the record it owns (`ClassroomRecordService`), not
the caller — the name must still make sense with every other class deleted. One
internal type may serve more than one contracted service.
